# Infrastructure + deploy

## Self-hosted mesh infra (off-ISP VPS) — do NOT reintroduce public deps

Both live on the OVH VPS (`51.81.33.184`, alongside coturn + Postfix), because
public infrastructure proved unreliable and the home router won't hairpin:

- **Signaling** (peer discovery / SDP): self-hosted **mosquitto** MQTT-over-WSS
  at `wss://signal.quasarke.net/mqtt` (mosquitto on localhost:8084 behind nginx
  TLS on :443 — mosquitto can't bind privileged ports, and the OVH firewall only
  passes a few TCP ports). Public MQTT brokers stalled SDP exchange → peers never
  connected. Env: `VITE_RELAY_URLS`. IaC: homelab `mail-stack/vps-relay/signaling`.
- **STUN/TURN**: self-hosted **coturn** at `turn:51.81.33.184:3478` (UDP). Client
  points at it **by IP** (no DNS at gather time). Env: `VITE_TURN_*`.
  IaC: homelab `mail-stack/vps-relay/coturn`.
- **NO third-party STUN/brokers** (no Google/Cloudflare/AWS) — this was an
  explicit product decision. Don't add them back "for reliability."

### DNS gotcha (split-horizon)
`*.quasarke.net` resolves to the internal `.88` Caddy on the LAN and to public
IPs externally. A VPS-hosted service therefore needs a name pinned to the VPS
from **both** horizons (public A record + a specific AdGuard rewrite overriding
the wildcard). `signal.quasarke.net → 51.81.33.184` is set up this way. WebSocket
also requires HTTP/1.1 through nginx (h2/ALPN breaks the Upgrade).

## Deploy (manual — no CD credential on the shared edge)

`legion.codecai.net` serves `apps/chat` at `/`, `apps/demo` at `/classic/`, from
ONE `legion-chat` container on `.198` (nginx-proxy + acme-companion; routes by
hostname not path, so both apps ship in one image, demo built `--base=/classic/`).

1. `scripts/prepare-deploy-context.sh` — materialize `codec-local/` +
   `.deploy-context/legion-stage-runtime/` as REAL files. On Windows checkouts the
   sibling-repo symlinks materialize as text stubs — **don't rsync them over a
   host that already has good copies.**
2. Ensure `.198:/storage/unstable-legion/.env` has real `VITE_TURN_*` +
   `VITE_RELAY_URLS`. **A missing `.env` silently builds a STUN-only / public-broker
   bundle — no error.**
3. `docker compose build legion-chat` → `scripts/verify-turn-baked.sh`
   (fails loud if TURN isn't baked) → `docker compose up -d legion-chat`.
4. Verify live: the running bundle greps for `turn:51.81.33.184` and
   `signal.quasarke.net`; a fresh peer reaches `checking→connected`.

Model weights are NOT in the image (host `webllm-mirror` volume, served `/webllm/`).

## Source-of-truth + persistence rules

- **Forgejo is a read-only mirror.** Commit to **GitHub `main`**
  (`git@github.com:wdunn001/Unstable-legion.git`).
- **Persist every host-side infra change to homelab IaC** (`homelab-compose`) in
  the same task — host edits drift and get wiped otherwise.
- **Secrets** (TURN credential, etc.) never enter chat/context/commits — read
  them server-side from the `.env`/conf in-shell; the leaked coturn cred is
  pending rotation.
